// REQUIRES: long
// P04.05: lowering strings, slices, views and maps is near-linear in every
// dimension a program can grow in: here a long `+` chain and big slice, map
// and string literals (core-stress-str-2: a deep chain of slicing, many
// slicing statements; core-stress-str-3: many map operations, many ranges
// over a map with their break, continue, return and goto exits, many appends
// and conversions); 4N takes at most 12 times as long as N. The control
// (core-stress-str-4) lowers a program whose size is the product of two
// dimensions and must fail the same check. The normal suite counts the work
// instead (tests/unit/GIR/StressTest.cpp): the GIR made
// (GIRStress.Lowering*IsLinear) and the steps of the lowering walks that make
// no GIR statement each (GIRStress.TheLoweringCounts*, gir::loweringSteps,
// one dimension grown 16 times, with a quadratic labelPos as the control).
// RUN: timeout 300 %gopp_unit_tests --gtest_also_run_disabled_tests --gtest_filter='GIRStressLong.DISABLED_LoweringConcatsAndLiterals'
